{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/35213-people-with-interesting-faces","id":35213,"title":"People with Interesting Faces","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-22T17:27:52-08:00","id":35213,"title":"People with Interesting Faces","content":"So this is something I'm always thinking about when I watch television shows and movies, I'm always looking to see who has features that are really striking and memorable. Frequently those people might wind up serving as visual inspiration for characters or NPCs in my games. I'm thinking this thread could be a place where we share some photos or names of actors, actresses or just public figures out there who have features that are memorable for one reason or another. Maybe they inspire you for your games, maybe you just think they look cool, do share!<br /> <br /> As an aside, I feel like I should try to make it clear that this isn't about just posting people we think are attractive or anything like that. Somebody could be very unattractive or attractive or middling, as long as they have features you find particularly memorable.<br /> <br /> Although I guess this one might be debated, but I've always thought <a href=\"http://www1.pictures.zimbio.com/gi/Mark+Strong+Inception+UK+film+Premiere+Outside+G0gp9SrsAGpl.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Mark Strong</a> had very striking features. There's an intensity to his gaze that really helps sell me on why people might pick him for the various media he's worked on. I'm particularly keen on using his features in a World of Darkness game I'm working on. <a href=\"http://trialx.com/curetalk/wp-content/blogs.dir/7/files/2011/04/gcelebrities/Michael_K__Williams-1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Michael K. Williams</a>'s another guy who I think has really interesting features, particularly the scar that he has. I recall reading the story behind it in an interview once, and I'm glad it's been something that has born some fruit when it comes to his career. We see a looter fake scars or makeup scars in movies, the real deal can serve as powerful visual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 12-22-2013, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T18:23:04-08:00","id":35243,"title":"","content":"I find <a href=\"http://trialx.com/curetalk/wp-content/blogs.dir/7/files/2011/04/gcelebrities/Saul_Rubinek-3.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Saul Rubinek</a> pretty memorable, but that could just be in contrast to the 'standard' TV face. Also <a href=\"http://images3.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20080315224328/firefly/images/9/93/Jewel_Staite-7814.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Jewel Staite</a> or <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><a href=\"http://scifipulse.net/wp-content/uploads/2013/06/Burn-Gorman.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Burn Gorman</a>'s faces tend to stick in my brain. Also I find using <a href=\"http://www.contactmusic.com/pics/la/zohan_premiere_2_290508/bree_turner_1890842.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Bree Turner </a>as inspiration if I want someone 'cute' works pretty well. And Nicholas Hope is just plain evil-looking: <a href=\"http://www.rideontheatre.com/wp-content/uploads/2010/10/nicholas-right-sized.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">doesn't this look like someone who'd engineer mass death</a>?<br /> <br /> Edit: Changed the links. Worked fine for me when I tested them, but these shouldn't cause a problem...hopefully.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","user":"Allan53","date":".  Fixing problem links 12-22-2013, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T18:33:16-08:00","id":35252,"title":"","content":"Your IMDB Hotlinks seem to be getting denied!<br /> <br /> I just saw Saul Rubinek in Leverage awhile ago. It was weird having him be antagonistic after being used to him being a decently good guy in Warehouse 13.<br /> <br /> There's something about <a href=\"http://images1.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20120922211618/supernatural/images/7/7b/Benny.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Ty Olsson</a>'s smirk that really sticks in my head. Whenever I'm trying to pick NPCs, I'll admit I'm usually playing a game like Vampire or now, Demon. When I'm looking for characters for that, I like actors and actresses of all kinds, but I'm particularly keen on those who have a serious or malevolent edge to their expression in the photo I get. That smirk could have a predatory gleam, y'know? (Rather fitting, what with Benny being what he is...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}